WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.050
Welcome to this module of The Water We Swim In,

2
00:00:03.250 --> 00:00:06.050
part of the People, Access and Culture learning program at

3
00:00:06.050 --> 00:00:09.170
the Minnesota Department of Human Services. This one is called

4
00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:12.030
Seen from the other side. It asks how Minnesota's majority

5
00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:14.770
culture looks to people who stand partly outside it.

6
00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:17.940
And it starts with a joke. A newcomer from Fargo

7
00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:20.760
was warned that Minnesotans will give you directions to anywhere

8
00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:23.660
except their own house. Most of us laugh, because we

9
00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:25.820
know that person. Friendly, helpful, means well.

10
00:00:26.430 --> 00:00:30.250
Right. And the newcomer may still drive away feeling like

11
00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:32.810
a guest. A culture looks one way from inside and

12
00:00:32.810 --> 00:00:33.750
another way from outside.

13
00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:37.060
I like how the module frames the goal. It isn't

14
00:00:37.060 --> 00:00:39.540
