18
00:00:46.510 --> 00:00:49.250
them speaks for a whole community. One that stayed with

19
00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:52.410
me is Arthur McWatt, a St. Paul native and retired

20
00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:56.090
social studies teacher, speaking in a 2002 public radio documentary.

21
00:00:56.900 --> 00:01:00.740
He described employers who accepted a Black applicant's application and

22
00:01:00.740 --> 00:01:03.580
then threw it away. He called it discrimination done in

23
00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:05.720
a more subtle way than in the South. And he

24
00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:09.360
said Black Minnesotans developed an antenna for insincerity, because racism

25
00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:12.000
here often came with a smile and a polite voice.

